course: dictionary
lesson: 3490
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which meaning the writer wants. «A wild goldfish has one tail fin; a fantail has a doubled tail, two tail fins side by side joined at the front.» The words goldfish and tail fin are the clues, so this fantail is a fancy fish, not a bird.
explain: Fantail has three main meanings: a small bird whose tail spreads out like a fan, a fancy pigeon or goldfish with a fan-shaped tail, and any tail or end shaped like a fan. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it talks about birds, pigeons or goldfish, that tells you which meaning fits.
explain: In New Zealand the fantail is a common, friendly bird, called pīwakawaka in Māori, that follows walkers to catch insects. The words friendly and follows show it is tame and close to people. Try each meaning in the sentence and keep the one that makes sense.
fact: A fantail is a small bird with a tail that spreads out like a fan.
fact: «Fantail» also means a fancy pigeon or goldfish with a fan-shaped tail.
fact: In New Zealand the fantail is called pīwakawaka in Māori.
fact: Fantail goldfish and fantail pigeons are bred as pets.
fact: A word with several meanings is called a multiple-meaning word, and the context shows which meaning is used.
exercise: «A wild goldfish has one tail fin; a fantail has a doubled tail, two tail fins side by side joined at the front.» In this sentence, what is a fantail? | *A fancy goldfish with a fan-shaped tail | A small bird | A tail shaped like a fan on a bird | A kind of wild fish with one fin
exercise: On a walk in New Zealand, a small bird follows you to catch insects. What is it? | *A fantail | A pigeon | A goldfish | A robin
exercise: A baker shapes the pastry edge into a fantail. What does fantail mean here? | A kind of bread roll | *A shape like an open fan | A small bird | A fish with one fin
test: Pīwakawaka is the Māori name for which bird? | *The fantail | A robin | A goldfish | A pigeon
test: «A fantail pigeon» is a pet pigeon. What is special about its tail? | It is as long as a snake | It has one tiny fin | It has no tail at all | *It spreads out like a fan
exam: Read: «Fantail goldfish are bred as pets.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | A small bird that catches insects, because it is found in New Zealand | A tail shaped like a fan on a wild bird | A pigeon, because pigeons are pets | *A fancy goldfish with a fan-shaped tail, because the sentence says pets and goldfish
